<title>JAPAN: SNCF launches 50 bln yen 5.4% yen/dlr samurai.</title>
<headline>SNCF launches 50 bln yen 5.4% yen/dlr samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Yamaichi Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Societe Nationale des Chemins de Fer Francais</p>
<p>			(SNCF)</p>
<p> AMT		 50 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.4 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  10 May 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  30 April 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 14 to April 28</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aa1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Yamaichi Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at $3,944.77 per 500,000 yen. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
